flowchart TD
    A([Issue in Triage]) --> B[Owner bot writes options]
    B --> C{Human decides in a comment,<br/>or moves the issue}
    C -->|owner bot has questions,<br/>issue not moved to Active| Q[Questions on the issue,<br/>issue stays in Triage]
    Q --> C
    C -->|brief written,<br/>card to Backlog| D[Coordinator starts worker]
    C -->|moves the issue to Active| D
    D --> D2[Worker pushes<br/>a first commit]
    D2 --> D3[Coordinator opens draft PR<br/>with a closing link,<br/>issue card stays in Active<br/>or moves to Active]
    D3 --> E[Worker pushes code and tests<br/>to the draft PR]
    E --> F{Coordinator<br/>pre-check}
    F -->|fails| E
    F -->|passes| G[Mark ready,<br/>card to Auto Review]
    G --> H{Automated review,<br/>round within the limit}
    H -->|P1 or P2 finding| I[Back to draft, In Progress,<br/>worker fixes the root cause,<br/>neighboring cases + tests]
    I --> J[Coordinator examines the fix,<br/>resolves the thread]
    J -->|under the limit| G
    J -->|limit reached:<br/>coordinator examines,<br/>no more automated rounds| K
    H -->|clean| K{Coordinator<br/>post-check}
    K --> L[Best-effort merge into staging,<br/>deploy staging,<br/>screenshots in the PR if visible]
    L --> M{Gate into Human Review,<br/>Linux checks green}
    M -->|passes, slot open| N[Human Review,<br/>two slots]
    M -->|passes, no slot| P[Pending queue]
    P -->|slot opens| N
    M -->|fails| I
    N -->|human moves card to In Progress,<br/>or late finding| I
    N -->|human merges| O([Main])
